# Comment blocks over the 10-line limit, frozen 2026-09-15 when this repo turned
# the hub's --ratchets on. Owner directive (hub AGENTS.md priority 6): two lines
# at the point of use, longer text into docs/ with a pointer. These seven predate
# the gate; the freeze is what makes it refuse the EIGHTH.
#
# Format: <file>	<first comment line>. Two-way: shrink a block under the limit
# and its row here goes STALE, so delete the row in the same commit.
# third_party/ANTfrastructure/docs/code-quality-tooling.md#comment-size-comment-size
#
# Six of the seven are file headers whose subject is WHY THE FILE IS A WRAPPER --
# what upstream owns, what was measured before delegating, and which upstream
# line the wrapper deliberately does not re-fork. That argument belongs next to
# the delegation it justifies, not in a docs page nobody opens while reading a
# 5-line script. antfrastructure.sh's two blocks are not this repo's prose at
# all: it is a body-mode copy of the hub's own template
# (.antfrastructure-shared.manifest), so shortening them would drift the
# shared-config gate instead.

benchmarks/ci-contract-tests.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
scripts/linux/ci-image-ref.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
scripts/linux/ci_static_analysis.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
scripts/linux/lib/antfrastructure.sh	# Replace this process with a ANTfrastructure driver, forwar
scripts/linux/lib/antfrastructure.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
scripts/linux/renovate-local.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
scripts/linux/run-lint-gates.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
